<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka opens firmer against dollar.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka opens firmer against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka opened firmer at 43.7460/7500 to the dollar in interba.7485/7495, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers expect the taka to retain the edge as a rise in call money rates may tempt banks to offload dollars, they said.</p>
<p>Some early deals were done at 43.7470 per dollar.</p>
<p>- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
